{"scenario": {"window_size": "1440x900", "description": "threads whose file left the review (PLAN §8, DESIGN §4.1): the reviewer comments (through the CLI) on an untracked file the agent then deletes, on a file the agent reverts, and on one that stays; opened, the two head the stream in its \"Not in the diff\" section as full cards (the deleted file's outdated, the reverted file's found in it, edited, with View file) and come first in the comments list; one is resolved from its row's right-click menu, the other answered through the menu's Reply and resolved from its card, the agent replies through the CLI; after Request changes the empty interdiff keeps the section (the empty state a row under it, its cards answering `R`), and once the agent edits again the interdiff still shows it. Screenshots in dark Mica and one light."}}
{"cmd": "wait_ready", "timeout_ms": 20000}
{"cmd": "set_setting", "key": "mode", "value": "dark"}
{"cmd": "settle"}

// The agent's work: a new hook (untracked), an edit to a file that is in the base, and one
// more edit that stays.
{"cmd": "seed_repo", "name": "web", "steps": [{"write": "src/hooks/use-auth.ts", "text": "export function useAuth() {\n  return { user: null };\n}\n"}, {"write": "src/lib/format.ts", "text": "export function format(value: number) {\n  return value.toFixed(2);\n}\n"}, {"commit": "base"}, {"write": "src/hooks/use-can.ts", "text": "import { useAuth } from \"./use-auth\";\n\nexport function useCan(permission: string) {\n  const { user } = useAuth();\n  return user?.permissions.includes(permission) ?? false;\n}\n"}, {"write": "src/lib/format.ts", "text": "export function format(value: number) {\n  return value.toFixed(3);\n}\n"}, {"write": "src/hooks/use-auth.ts", "text": "export function useAuth() {\n  return { user: null as null | { permissions: string[] } };\n}\n"}]}
{"cmd": "cli", "cwd": "repos/web", "args": ["review", "new", "--json"], "expect_result": {"pointer": "/exit", "equals": 0}}
{"cmd": "cli", "cwd": "repos/web", "args": ["comment", "add", "--file", "src/hooks/use-can.ts", "--lines", "5", "--body", "A missing user should throw, not read as \"no permission\".", "--json"], "save": {"t1": "/json/thread/id"}, "expect_result": [{"pointer": "/exit", "equals": 0}, {"pointer": "/json/thread/placement", "equals": "unchanged"}]}
{"cmd": "cli", "cwd": "repos/web", "args": ["comment", "add", "--file", "src/lib/format.ts", "--lines", "2", "--body", "Why three decimals?", "--json"], "save": {"t2": "/json/thread/id"}, "expect_result": [{"pointer": "/exit", "equals": 0}, {"pointer": "/json/thread/placement", "equals": "unchanged"}]}
{"cmd": "cli", "cwd": "repos/web", "args": ["comment", "add", "--file", "src/hooks/use-auth.ts", "--lines", "2", "--body", "Type the user once, in types.ts.", "--json"], "save": {"t3": "/json/thread/id"}, "expect_result": {"pointer": "/exit", "equals": 0}}
// The agent deletes the hook (it was never committed) and reverts format.ts: both files leave
// the review's list, and their threads with them (PLAN §8): the hook's is outdated (its file is
// gone), format.ts's is found in the reverted file, edited where it stood, not in the diff.
{"cmd": "repo_edit", "name": "web", "steps": [{"remove": "src/hooks/use-can.ts"}, {"write": "src/lib/format.ts", "text": "export function format(value: number) {\n  return value.toFixed(2);\n}\n"}]}
{"cmd": "cli", "cwd": "repos/web", "args": ["comment", "list", "--json"], "env": {"CLAUDECODE": "1"}, "expect_result": [{"pointer": "/exit", "equals": 0}, {"pointer": "/json/threads/0/id", "equals": "${t1}"}, {"pointer": "/json/threads/0/placement", "equals": "outdated"}, {"pointer": "/json/threads/0/in_diff", "equals": false}, {"pointer": "/json/threads/1/placement", "equals": "edited"}, {"pointer": "/json/threads/1/in_diff", "equals": false}, {"pointer": "/json/threads/1/anchor/current/start_line", "equals": 2}, {"pointer": "/json/threads/2/placement", "equals": "unchanged"}, {"pointer": "/json/threads/2/in_diff", "equals": true}]}

// Opened: one file, and the section heading the stream with the two cards, in the order they
// were added; the comments list names them first: the hook's flagged outdated, where it was
// written, format.ts's where it stands in the file the review doesn't change now.
{"cmd": "open_review", "path": "${data_dir}/repos/web"}
{"cmd": "wait_for", "pointer": "/session/total", "equals": 1}
{"cmd": "settle", "expect": [{"pointer": "/session/files/0/path", "equals": "src/hooks/use-auth.ts"}, {"pointer": "/stream/not_in_diff", "equals": {"collapsed": false, "threads": ["${t1}", "${t2}"], "empty": null}}, {"pointer": "/stream/files", "len": 1}, {"pointer": "/stream/top_file", "equals": null}, {"pointer": "/session/threads/0/placement", "equals": "outdated"}, {"pointer": "/session/threads/1/placement", "equals": "edited"}, {"pointer": "/session/threads/1/in_diff", "equals": false}, {"pointer": "/session/threads/1/lines", "equals": {"start": 2, "end": 2}}, {"pointer": "/session/threads/2/placement", "equals": "unchanged"}, {"pointer": "/comments_list/rows/0/id", "equals": "${t1}"}, {"pointer": "/comments_list/rows/0/location", "equals": "src/hooks/use-can.ts:5"}, {"pointer": "/comments_list/rows/0/outdated", "equals": true}, {"pointer": "/comments_list/rows/1/id", "equals": "${t2}"}, {"pointer": "/comments_list/rows/1/location", "equals": "src/lib/format.ts:2"}, {"pointer": "/comments_list/rows/1/outdated", "equals": false}, {"pointer": "/comments_list/rows/2/id", "equals": "${t3}"}, {"pointer": "/shell/empty_state", "equals": null}]}
{"cmd": "query", "prefix": "stream/not_in_diff/", "expect_result": {"pointer": "", "len": 2}}
{"cmd": "query", "prefix": "thread/${t1}/resolve", "expect_result": {"pointer": "", "len": 1}}
// The card found in the unchanged file offers its file view; the gone one doesn't.
{"cmd": "query", "prefix": "thread/${t2}/view_file", "expect_result": {"pointer": "", "len": 1}}
{"cmd": "query", "prefix": "thread/${t1}/view_file", "expect_result": {"pointer": "", "len": 0}}
{"cmd": "screenshot", "name": "section-dark-mica"}

